Adapt to http2 5.x without returning streamed bodies from H.run's callback:
H.run drains queued DATA when that callback returns, while SimpleX passes
the body reader to another thread. Use the explicit stream-ownership API;
normal body reads still update flow-control windows. The optional Aux
stream/ping helpers are not used by SimpleX.

Own setup workers across cancellation and failed acquisition, and unmask
their bodies even when the caller brackets client creation. Error publication
must not block behind an already published client. Join workers on failure
and close with interruptible cancel so TLS shutdown deadlines can fire.

